#
# apps/examples/desktop_companion/Kconfig
#
# Kconfig for the AI-VOX3 desktop companion example application.
#
# NOTE: To be picked up by the build, this file must be sourced from
# apps/examples/Kconfig (add:  source "examples/desktop_companion/Kconfig").
# See staging/README.md for the exact integration steps.
#

config EXAMPLES_DESKTOP_COMPANION
  tristate "Desktop Companion (AI-VOX3) example"
  default n
  ---help---
    AI-VOX3 desktop companion application: 5 facial expressions, time/weather/
    todo desktop cards, a text->LLM(mimo-v2.5-pro)->echo loop, a servo-based
    face-follow demo (no camera), and a smart-home intent stub.

  if EXAMPLES_DESKTOP_COMPANION

  config AIVOX3_LLM_API_KEY
    string "LLM API key (injected at build; NEVER commit plaintext)"
    default ""
    ---help---
      API key for the mimo-v2.6-pro endpoint. Leave empty to inject it at
      runtime via NVS. The source tree MUST NOT contain the real secret;
      prefer menuconfig or an NVS-stored value.

  config AIVOX3_LLM_MODEL
    string "LLM model name"
    default "mimo-v2.6-pro"

  config AIVOX3_WIFI_SSID
    string "Wi-Fi SSID (station mode)"
    default ""
    ---help---
      SSID of the AP the board associates with at boot. net_init() reads it
      when net_wifi_connect() is called with a NULL/empty ssid, which is
      what main.c does.

      Leave it empty only if the network is joined some other way (e.g. the
      esp32s3 saved-parameter auto-join); with an empty value net_init()
      fails fast with -EINVAL and says so in the syslog instead of hanging.

  config AIVOX3_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "Wi-Fi WPA2 passphrase (build-config only; NEVER commit plaintext)"
    default ""
    ---help---
      WPA2-PSK passphrase for the SSID above. Like AIVOX3_LLM_API_KEY this is
      a build-time symbol: set it with menuconfig or inject it at build time,
      and never hard-code it in a .c/.h file. The source tree carries only the
      empty default.

      net_services.c logs the SSID and the fact that a passphrase is set, but
      NEVER the passphrase itself.

  config AIVOX3_BRIDGE_HOST
    string "PC voice bridge host (IP of the machine running bridge_chat.py)"
    default "192.168.1.23"
    ---help---
      The board has no ASR and no TTS, so a spoken turn is relayed to a PC
      running toolchain/voice_bridge/bridge_chat.py (Vosk ASR + mimo LLM +
      edge-tts), which listens on 0.0.0.0:8765.

      THIS ADDRESS WILL GO STALE: home routers hand out DHCP leases, so the
      PC moves. Set the value that is correct for your LAN here, and use the
      console command below after flashing when it changes:

          bridge 192.168.1.42        (same port)
          bridge 192.168.1.42 9000   (host + port)

      Typing "bridge" alone on the USB-CDC console prints the endpoint
      currently in use. The runtime override is RAM-only (lost on reboot).

  config AIVOX3_BRIDGE_PORT
    int "PC voice bridge TCP port"
    default 8765
    range 1 65535

  config AIVOX3_BRIDGE_TIMEOUT
    int "PC voice bridge timeout (seconds of socket inactivity)"
    default 60
    range 10 300
    ---help---
      One turn costs Vosk/mimo ASR (1-4 s) + streaming LLM (3-10 s) +
      per-sentence TTS (2-6 s). This is an INACTIVITY timeout restarted by
      every received burst, not an overall deadline, so 60 s is a safe
      default that only fires on a genuinely dead bridge.

  config SMART_HOME_BACKEND
    string "Smart-home backend (none/mqtt/http)"
    default "none"
    ---help---
      Selects the smart-home backend. The default "none" makes
      smart_home_control() parse intent and return "unconfigured".

  config AIVOX3_KWS_STORE_PATH
    string "Offline wake-word template storage path"
    default "/mnt/sd0/wake.bin"
    ---help---
      POSIX path used by kws_save()/kws_load() to persist the DTW template
      bank. It MUST point into a writable, mounted filesystem (FAT on the
      SD card or on a SPI-flash partition). This board config currently
      enables no writable filesystem, so kws_save() will report -ENOENT
      until one is mounted; templates then live in RAM only.

  config AIVOX3_KWS_THRESHOLD
    int "Default DTW decision threshold (0 = wait for calibration)"
    default 2400
    ---help---
      Normalized DTW distance below which an utterance is accepted. 2400 is
      the value measured on the Arduino reference firmware after recording
      "ni hao, openvela" three times; it transfers directly because the
      front-end geometry, feature scaling and distance metric are identical.
      Set 0 to require kws_learn() to calibrate a threshold first.

  config AIVOX3_READ_ENABLED
    bool "Audiobook (novel reading) mode"
    default y
    ---help---
      Adds the "read the novel" feature: load a novel text from FFat, send each
      segment to the PC bridge /tts endpoint and play the returned PCM through
      the existing chat TTS path. Trigger via the serial 'read' command, an
      LVGL "READ" button, or 'pause'/'resume'/'next'/'prev'/'stop' to control
      playback.

  config AIVOX3_READ_NOVEL_PATH
    string "Novel file path on FFat"
    default "/mnt/ffat/novel.txt"
    depends on AIVOX3_READ_ENABLED
    ---help---
      POSIX path the reader opens for the novel text (and writes the built-in
      sample to on first boot). Must resolve inside a mounted, writable FFat.

  config AIVOX3_READ_NOVEL_MAX_BYTES
    int "Max novel size loaded into RAM (bytes)"
    default 262144
    range 8192 4194304
    depends on AIVOX3_READ_ENABLED
    ---help---
      Upper bound on the novel bytes loaded into RAM. The reading feature is
      intended for short stories / chapters; the bridge /upload_novel enforces
      the same ceiling on the PC side.

  endif
